WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.435
Governance in Active Directory
was mostly a ticket queue:

2
00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:07.525
someone asked for membership, someone
added it, and nobody took it away.

3
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:09.713
The target replaces that with a loop.

4
00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:13.376
HR-driven provisioning creates
and updates the account.

5
00:00:13.376 --> 00:00:17.625
Lifecycle Workflows run the
joiner, mover and leaver tasks.

6
00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:20.763
Access packages grant
access with an expiry.

7
00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:24.137
And access reviews remove
what's no longer justified.

8
00:00:24.137 --> 00:00:28.924
Lifecycle Workflows act on accounts that
already exist; they don't create them.

9
00:00:28.924 --> 00:00:32.875
The time-based triggers key on
the native employee hire date and

10
00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:36.975
leave date attributes, with an offset
of up to a hundred eighty days.

11
00:00:36.975 --> 00:00:41.712
For synced users, those dates must
be synced into Entra ID first.

12
00:00:41.712 --> 00:00:46.931
Pre-hire runs seven days before the hire
date: confirm the account exists, disabled;

13
00:00:46.931 --> 00:00:49.463
request the onboarding access package;

14
00:00:49.463 --> 00:00:53.301
and generate a Temporary Access
Pass emailed to the manager,

15
00:00:53.301 --> 00:00:57.675
so the new hire registers a
phishing-resistant credential on day one.

16
00:00:57.675 --> 00:01:02.154
Joiner runs on the day: enable the
account, assign licenses by group,

17
00:01:02.154 --> 00:01:05.900
send the welcome email,
request the department package.

18
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.696
Mover fires on a change to department,
division code or position category:

19
00:01:10.696 --> 00:01:14.313
remove the old department's
package, request the new one,

20
00:01:14.313 --> 00:01:19.738
let dynamic groups and a dynamic administrative
unit adjust, and review what's left.

21
00:01:19.738 --> 00:01:22.944
Leaver runs on the leave
date: disable the account,

22
00:01:22.944 --> 00:01:25.213
revoke refresh and session tokens,

23
00:01:25.213 --> 00:01:29.985
remove access packages and then licenses
after the mailbox is converted,

24
00:01:29.985 --> 00:01:33.975
remove group memberships at
thirty days and delete at ninety.

25
00:01:33.975 --> 00:01:35.138
Two cautions.

26
00:01:35.138 --> 00:01:38.911
The delete task doesn't support
users holding Entra roles or

27
00:01:38.911 --> 00:01:43.288
role-assignable group membership,
so remove privileged access first.

28
00:01:43.288 --> 00:01:46.166
And a synced user
deleted only in the cloud

29
00:01:46.166 --> 00:01:48.962
comes back on the next
sync; delete it in AD.

30
00:01:48.962 --> 00:01:50.550
Reviews close the loop.

31
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:55.457
PIM-eligible role assignments are
reviewed quarterly by the security team,

32
00:01:55.457 --> 00:01:59.273
not by self-review, which leaves
role-assignable groups out;

33
00:01:59.273 --> 00:02:02.700
that review is the AC-6(7) evidence.

34
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.390
Sensitive groups go quarterly to
owners, guests quarterly to sponsors.
